- [ ] Consider removing TypeScript ops where we have WASM and have WASM run all cases
- [ ] Add JS benchmarks to docs
- [ ] Add JS-vs-WASM differential tests: for each op, run both backends (`wasmConfig.thresholdMultiplier` = `Infinity` vs `0`) on the same random input and compare bitwise or within an ulp tolerance. In-process, no Python, fast.
    - Sweep sizes 0..70 so lengths land on and around every SIMD lane width (catches scalar tail-loop bugs)
    - Include offset / misaligned views, not just fresh contiguous arrays
    - Today only `tests/validation/dtype-sweep/` runs under `FORCE_BACKEND`; most unit tests use small arrays and never reach WASM
- [ ] Add property-based / metamorphic tests with `fast-check` (not a dependency yet)
    - Invariants: `transpose(transpose(a)) == a`, reshape round-trip, sum over each axis == total sum, `fft(ifft(x)) ≈ x`, sort idempotent, broadcasting symmetric in operand order, dtype promotion symmetric
    - Generate random shapes, strides, and offset/non-contiguous views to hit layout bugs hand-picked cases miss
    - Follow-up: feed the same generators into `runNumPyBatch()` for randomized NumPy differential testing (pinned seed + small case count in CI, larger nightly run)
